<equipmentSetData xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="common.xsd">
	<defaults/>

	<!--
	Rapport: take the WEAPONS off and leave everything else alone.

	Why this file exists. AAF's own "unEquip" set already lists all twelve
	"Possibly Weapons" biped slots, so on any scene where AAF undresses, a
	visible-holstered-weapons mod's rig comes off with the clothes. The gap is the
	CLOTHED scene: a cuddle or a kiss never triggers undressing at all, so the
	rifle stays strapped to their back, through the whole animation.

	So this is AAF's unEquip set with every clothing entry removed. Slots 33 to 44,
	which the Creation Kit leaves unnamed and AAF calls "Possibly Weapons1" through
	"Possibly Weapons12", are where visible-weapon mods mount their meshes. Nothing
	here touches BODY, the [U] and [A] armour slots, hair, or anything else a
	dressed actor is wearing.

	Why it goes through AAF rather than Papyrus. Actor has UnequipItemSlot(int) but
	the base game's Papyrus has NO GetWornItem, so a mod that unequips a slot
	itself cannot read what was in it and cannot put it back. Removing somebody's
	gear with no way to restore it is not acceptable, and AAF's equipmentSet
	machinery already does the save and restore properly.

	Paired with AAF's stock "reEquip" set as the stop set. That one is
	reEquip resetAll="true" and restores whatever was taken.

	NOTE, still being tested: whether naming a start set SUPPRESSES AAF's normal
	undressing is not knowable from any source. The settings struct declares
	startEquipmentSet and GetPositionSettings defaults it to None, but the handling
	is in the DLL, the same place the position trees live. If clothes stop coming
	off on ordinary scenes, that is this file, and HolsterWeapons = 0 in
	Rapport.ini turns the whole thing off in one line.
	-->

	<equipmentSet id="Rapport_WeaponsOnly">
		<condition>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons1"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons2"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons3"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons4"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons5"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons6"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons7"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons8"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons9"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons10"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons11"/>
			<unEquip bipedSlot="Possibly Weapons12"/>
		</condition>
	</equipmentSet>
</equipmentSetData>
